<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mithridates I Callinicus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 109–70 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mithridates-i-of-parthia">Mithridates I</a> Callinicus was king of Commagene, in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, from about 109 to 70 BCE. He married Laodice, daughter of the Seleucid king Antiochus VIII, uniting Persian and Macedonian royal lines, a double heritage that his son and successor Antiochus I Theos celebrated in his royal cult and monuments.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mithridates-i-callinicus.jpg" alt="Mithridates I Callinicus" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rudolf B · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arsameia_Mithridates_I_R0013704.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
